{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["The reason for <b>to all the congregation of the children of Israel:</b> to include the converts, because they are cautioned regarding forbidden relations just as the Israelites." "And the reason this pericope is mentioned after the forbidden relations: lest they think that because of observance of the forbidden relations alone they will endure in the land, He told them that there are also other commandments — if you do not observe them you will be expelled from the land. They are the Ten Commandments mentioned here: for He cautioned against idolatry after saying 'for holy am I, HaShem,' for it corresponds to the first commandment according to many; and 'you shall not swear by My name' is the commandment 'you shall not take'; and 'you shall keep My Sabbaths' — 'remember the Sabbath day'; and 'you shall each revere his mother and father' is the commandment 'honor your father and your mother'; and 'you shall not stand by the blood of your fellow' is the commandment 'you shall not murder.' And the matter of the cursed maidservant is a warning against 'you shall not commit adultery,' even though she is a free woman. Also 'you shall not steal' and 'you shall not deny' and 'you shall not lie' and 'you shall not oppress your fellow' correspond to the three remaining."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:53.486008464Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}